{"id": "impl_agents_miss_stale_doc_refs", "type": "gotcha", "fact": "Implementation agents claim docs don't need updating while stale references remain in reference docs", "recommendation": "During gemini_hybrid_06_hard_cutover, the implementation agent reported docs/reference/data-model.md needed no changes, but the orchestrator found it still documented enableHybridPipeline and hybridPipelineRolloutPercentage fields that were removed from code. When removing code, always grep docs/ for references to removed exports, types, and config fields \u2014 implementation agents routinely miss this.", "confidence": "medium", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "gemini_hybrid_06_hard_cutover/iteration_01", "date": "2026-03-21"}], "tags": ["architecture-refactor"], "affectedFiles": [], "createdAt": "2026-03-21T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-03-21T00:00:00Z"}
{"id": "gcp_rest_api_can_unblock_ops_review_without_gcloud", "type": "gotcha", "fact": "Mounted gcloud auth state can be enough to verify and execute GCP cleanup even when the gcloud CLI is missing", "recommendation": "During gemini_hybrid_06_infra_cleanup/iteration_01_a, the environment lacked the `gcloud` binary but still had usable OAuth tokens in `~/.config/gcloud/access_tokens.db`. The implementation used direct GCP REST API calls to list resources, perform deletions, and capture before/after evidence. For ops-heavy scopes, missing gcloud does not automatically mean BLOCK if authenticated token state is present and can be used safely for explicit verification.", "confidence": "medium", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "gemini_hybrid_06_infra_cleanup/iteration_01_a", "date": "2026-03-22"}], "tags": ["architecture-refactor"], "affectedFiles": [], "createdAt": "2026-03-22T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-03-22T00:00:00Z"}
{"id": "cloud_run_node20_slim_needs_ca_certs_for_storage_downloads", "type": "gotcha", "fact": "`node:20-slim` Cloud Run images can hang on GCS downloads if `ca-certificates` is missing", "recommendation": "During gemini_hybrid_09_cloud_run_orchestrator_01_core/iteration_01_b, the orchestrator container could reach Firestore but Storage downloads stalled because the runtime image lacked `ca-certificates`. `@google-cloud/storage` ultimately used a Node HTTP stack that never surfaced a clear TLS error, while `curl` failed with certificate error 77. For Cloud Run services built from Debian slim images, install `ca-certificates` explicitly before debugging Storage/network hangs.", "confidence": "medium", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "gemini_hybrid_09_cloud_run_orchestrator_01_core/iteration_01_b", "date": "2026-03-25"}], "tags": ["architecture-refactor"], "affectedFiles": [], "createdAt": "2026-03-25T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-03-25T00:00:00Z"}
{"id": "conversation_id_log_filter_hides_infra_noise_by_design", "type": "gotcha", "fact": "Applying a conversation ID filter at the Cloud Logging query layer will drop infrastructure logs that do not mention that ID", "recommendation": "In gemini_hybrid_09_cloud_run_orchestrator_02_log_tooling/iteration_01, the approved implementation appended the conversation ID directly to the Cloud Logging query rather than post-filtering in Python. That improves signal when debugging a single run, but startup, health-check, and other platform entries disappear unless they contain the same ID. Document that trade-off in operator-facing help text whenever a scoped conversation filter is added to log tooling.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "gemini_hybrid_09_cloud_run_orchestrator_02_log_tooling/iteration_01", "date": "2026-03-27"}], "tags": ["architecture-refactor", "logging", "operators"], "affectedFiles": ["~/PycharmProjects/agent-process-central/audio-transcript-analysis-app/scripts/fetch-firebase-logs.py"], "createdAt": "2026-03-27T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-03-27T00:00:00Z"}
